# Sort Colors — LeetCode 75

**Pattern:** Three Pointers  
**Algorithm:** Dutch National Flag  
**Approach:** In-place swapping

## Approach
1. Initialize `low = 0`, `mid = 0`, `high = n - 1`.
2. If `nums[mid] == 0`: swap `nums[low]` and `nums[mid]`, then increment `low` and `mid`.
3. If `nums[mid] == 1`: increment `mid`.
4. If `nums[mid] == 2`: swap `nums[mid]` and `nums[high]`, then decrement `high`.
5. Repeat while `mid <= high`.

## Java Code

```java
class Solution {
    public void sortColors(int[] nums) {
        int low = 0, mid = 0, high = nums.length - 1;

        while (mid <= high) {
            if (nums[mid] == 0) {
                int temp = nums[low];
                nums[low] = nums[mid];
                nums[mid] = temp;
                low++;
                mid++;
            } else if (nums[mid] == 1) {
                mid++;
            } else {
                int temp = nums[mid];
                nums[mid] = nums[high];
                nums[high] = temp;
                high--;
            }
        }
    }
}
